# Contents rather than the directory: git will not un-ignore a file inside an ignored directory,
# so `analysis/models/` followed by a negation silently keeps ignoring the file and `git add`
# reports nothing. The trailing `*` is what makes the negation below reachable.
analysis/models/*
# Except the one model that ships. A tool whose language scoring needs a 2.4GB local build is a
# tool nobody can run from a clone, so a small transformer is committed and the large Kneser-Ney
# models stay build artifacts. See analysis/README.md for the size/quality trade.
!analysis/models/background.tf.gz
analysis/corpora/
